Vendor specific extensibility mechanisms can be used by a vendor or by an SDO. In the context of
O-RAN Alliance, the O-RAN Alliance community can use vendor specific extensibility mechanisms and define a new
standardized data model as O-RAN YANG modules. An O1 producer or consumer to be O1 compliant will have to
support new standardized data models.
Vendor extensions to a 3GPP YANG module can be done to:
1) Marking in a 3GPP YANG modules as “not supported” any optional element according to supportQualifier
and/or any deviations that maintain backward compatibility as defined in RFC 7950
Vendor extensions to a 3GPP YANG module shall be done in a separate YANG module using augmentation mechanism:
1) Add vendor specific attributes to a 3GPP specified IOC
2) Add a new vendor specific IOC
In case 2 and 3, the vendor extensions are name contained in an existing 3GPP IOC and the new IOC shall follow 3GPP
TS 32.160 [i.9] methodology.
3GPP TS 32.160 [i.9] provides examples of case 2) and 3) as follows:
Example 1 – Add a vendor specific attribute to a 3GPP specified IOC:
augment /me3gpp:ManagedElement/attributes {
leaf isCabinetClosed {
type boolean ;
description “Indicates whether the doors of the HW cabinet is closed.” ;
}
}
Example 2 – Add a vendor specific IOC:
//vendor class
grouping VendorClassGrp {

