}
}
O-RAN has already defined extensions to 3GPP YANG modules, applying 3GPP extensibility principles and has
provided O-RAN defined YANG modules. For example, the o-ran_3gpp-nr-nrm-gnbdufunction.yang module is an
extension of the 3gpp-nr-nrm-gnbdufunction.yang module where the attributes of the 3GPP
ManagedElement/gnbdu3gpp:GNBDUFunction IOC have been augemented with additional O-RAN specific attributes
(i.e. mac-configuration-group) to be used with O-RAN specific namespace (i.e. o-ran:oran-gnbdufunction). This is an
example of O-RAN Alliance extension of type 2) above.
